This repository is licensed in two parts.

  Source code    MIT — the full text below.
  Written and visual content    CC BY-NC 4.0 — see LICENSE-CONTENT.md.

The split exists because the two are not the same kind of work. The code is
meant to be copied, adapted and reused without asking. The writing, the
photographs and the visual studies are the archive itself, and reusing them
commercially is a different request.

WHAT THE MIT LICENSE BELOW COVERS

  Everything executable or structural: src/ except src/content/, scripts/,
  tests/, the build pipeline, configuration files, styles, and components.

WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER

  src/content/**            entries for Work, Lab, Notes and Gallery
  public/gallery/**         gallery media
  public/og/**              social cards
  assets/**                 brand marks and imagery
  Any prose rendered on the site

  These are CC BY-NC 4.0. See LICENSE-CONTENT.md.

  Third-party assets keep the licence they came with, and nothing here grants
  rights over them:

    public/fonts/switzer-variable.woff2        see SWITZER-LICENSE.txt
    public/fonts/ibm-plex-mono-regular.woff2   see IBM-PLEX-LICENSE.txt
    public/models/RobotExpressive.glb          CC0, by Tomás Laulhé
    public/models/NeilArmstrong.glb            see NeilArmstrong-Apache-2.0-LICENSE.txt
    public/models/RocketShip.glb               provenance not recorded

  Icons are resolved at build time from Lucide (ISC) and Simple Icons (CC0);
  both are development dependencies and neither ships to the browser.

